---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const SUPPORT = "support@lector.dev";
const LICENSE = "https://github.com/heuwels/lector/blob/master/LICENSE";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service | Lector"
  description="The terms governing the Lector software, this website, and the managed cloud service."
>
  <header class="docs-header">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">lector</a> / terms</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="post-meta">Last updated 20 August 2026</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="docs-body">
      <p>
        Lector is two things: open-source software you can run yourself, and a
        managed cloud service (coming soon) that runs it for you. These terms
        cover both, plus this website. By using Lector you agree to them.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>Short version.</strong> The self-hosted software is free and open
          source, provided as-is with no warranty. The cloud service, when available,
          is a paid subscription sold through Paddle; your data stays yours, and you
          can cancel any time. See the <a href="/refunds/">Refund Policy</a> and{" "}
          <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>1. The self-hosted software</h2>
      <p>
        Lector is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0
        (AGPL-3.0-only). Your rights to use, modify, and redistribute it are
        governed by that licence — read it in full{" "}
        <a href={LICENSE} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The software is provided <strong>&ldquo;as is&rdquo;, without warranty of
        any kind</strong>, express or implied, including but not limited to the
        warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
        non-infringement. When you self-host, you are responsible for your own
        deployment, your data and backups, and any third-party services or API
        keys you connect (and their costs). To the maximum extent permitted by
        law, the authors are not liable for any claim, damages, or other
        liability arising from the software or its use.
      </p>

      <h2>2. This website</h2>
      <p>
        This site is provided for information about Lector. We may change or
        update its content at any time. Links to third-party sites (GitHub,
        AnkiWeb, Discord, and others) are provided for convenience; we aren't
        responsible for their content.
      </p>

      <h2>3. The cloud service</h2>
      <p>
        The managed cloud service is not yet available. When it launches, the
        following will apply in addition to the terms above.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Billing.</strong> Subscriptions are sold and processed by
          Paddle.com Market Ltd, which acts as the merchant of record for your
          purchase. Paddle's own{" "}
          <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/checkout-buyer-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">buyer terms</a>
          {" "}also apply to the transaction. Refunds and cancellations are covered by
          our <a href="/refunds/">Refund Policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your data.</strong> Content you import, create, or translate
          remains yours. You grant us only the limited rights needed to operate
          the service for you — storing your data, and processing text through
          translation providers to return results. We don't sell your data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Acceptable use.</strong> Don't use the service to break the
          law, infringe others' rights, abuse the infrastructure, or resell
          access. Don't upload material you don't have the rights to. We may
          suspend or terminate accounts that do. Copyright holders can report
          infringing material and file a takedown via our{" "}
          <a href="/complaints/">complaints page</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Community library.</strong> If you submit a collection to the
          community catalog, you grant every signed-in user on that instance
          a licence to copy the frozen text into their own library. Lector may
          remove an item at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Availability.</strong> We aim for a reliable service but don't
          guarantee uninterrupted uptime. Features and plans may change with
          reasonable notice.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, Lector and its authors are not
        liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, or for any
        loss of data or profits, arising from your use of the software, this
        website, or the cloud service. Nothing in these terms excludes liability
        that cannot be excluded under applicable law, including your rights under
        the Australian Consumer Law.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the project and the cloud service evolve.
        Material changes will be reflected by the &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date
        above. Continued use after a change means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Email{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT}`}>{SUPPORT}</a>, or reach us on{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/heuwels/lector" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
        {" "}or <a href="https://discord.gg/XBEnx2ZWd5" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord</a>.
        You can also use the{" "}
        <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
        Lector is operated by Luke Boyle. These terms are governed by the laws of
        Australia.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
